Installation & Access Credentials Guide
Centralized Assessment Record System for GMA Child Development Center

================================================================================
SYSTEM OVERVIEW
================================================================================

Application Name: Centralized Assessment Record System
Version: Laravel 12 + React 19 + TypeScript
Repository: https://github.com/Rakanya-dev/laravel-project
Production URL: https://laravel-project-snowy-seven.vercel.app
Last Updated: August 2026

Technology Stack:
- Backend: Laravel 12 (PHP 8.2+)
- Frontend: React 19 with TypeScript (76.6%)
- Backend PHP: 19.5%
- Blade Templates: 2.6%
- Database: MySQL 5.7+ or SQLite (default)
- Build Tool: Vite 6
- UI Framework: Radix UI + Tailwind CSS 4

================================================================================
QUICK START - LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ACCESS
================================================================================

Frontend URL: http://localhost:5173
Backend URL: http://localhost:8000
Database: SQLite (database/database.sqlite)

Prerequisites:
- PHP 8.2 or higher
- Node.js 18.x or higher
- npm 10.x or higher
- Composer (latest)
- 2GB RAM minimum
- 500MB free disk space

================================================================================
INSTALLATION STEPS
================================================================================

Step 1: Clone Repository
Command: git clone https://github.com/Rakanya-dev/laravel-project.git
Command: cd laravel-project

Step 2: Install PHP Dependencies
Command: composer install

Step 3: Install Node.js Dependencies
Command: npm install

Step 4: Setup Environment File
Command: cp .env.example .env
Command: php artisan key:generate

Step 5: Configure Database (.env file)

Option A - SQLite (Default - No Setup Required):
DB_CONNECTION=sqlite
Database file auto-creates at: database/database.sqlite

Option B - MySQL (Production Recommended):
DB_CONNECTION=mysql
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=laravel
DB_USERNAME=root
DB_PASSWORD=(your password)
DB_CHARSET=utf8mb4
DB_COLLATION=utf8mb4_unicode_ci

Create MySQL Database:
mysql -u root -p
CREATE DATABASE laravel;
EXIT;

Step 6: Run Database Migrations & Seed Data
Command: php artisan migrate
Command: php artisan db:seed

Step 7: Build Frontend Assets
Command: npm run build (production)
Command: npm run dev (development with hot reload)

Step 8: Start Application

Option A - Run Everything Together (Recommended):
Command: npm run start

This launches:
- PHP Development Server (port 8000)
- Vite Development Server (port 5173)
- Queue Listener (background jobs)
- Laravel Reverb (WebSockets)

Option B - Run Services Separately:
Terminal 1: php artisan serve
Terminal 2: npm run dev
Terminal 3: php artisan queue:listen --tries=1

Step 9: Access Application
Open http://localhost:5173 in your web browser

