================================================================================
USER ROLES & ACCESS LEVELS
================================================================================

1. ADMINISTRATOR ROLE
Access Level: Full System Access

Permissions:
✓ View system-wide dashboard and metrics
✓ Manage all staff and user accounts
✓ Create and approve teacher accounts
✓ Manage daycare centers and sections
✓ Approve/reject student enrollments
✓ Verify enrollment documents
✓ Create and manage assessment domains
✓ Generate compliance and analytics reports
✓ Send messages to all users
✓ Archive/restore student and staff records
✓ Configure system settings
✓ View all user activity logs

Login Route: /admin/dashboard
Dashboard Metrics:
- Total learners and active learners
- Pending enrollment count
- Assessment completion rates
- Active staff count
- Recent user activity feed
- System health status

---

2. TEACHER (CDW) ROLE
Access Level: Limited to Assigned Students & Classes

Permissions:
✓ View assigned students in own section
✓ Create ECCD and ITED assessments
✓ Edit and mark assessments as complete
✓ Flag assessments for review
✓ View student assessment history
✓ Generate class reports
✓ Send messages to parents and admins
✓ Archive/restore student records
✓ Export class roster
✗ Cannot approve enrollments
✗ Cannot create daycares or sections
✗ Cannot manage other teachers
✗ Cannot create assessment domains
✗ Cannot import students via CSV

Login Route: /teacher/dashboard
Dashboard Metrics:
- Total students in assigned section
- Total assessments completed
- Pending assessments due
- Class average score
- Student roster by section

---

3. PARENT/GUARDIAN ROLE
Access Level: Limited to Own Children Only

Permissions:
✓ Create child enrollment
✓ Upload enrollment documents
✓ View child's assessment history
✓ Download and print report cards
✓ View child's progress and scores
✓ Send messages to teachers
✓ Link additional guardians to child
✓ Accept guardian link invitations
✓ Update profile information
✓ Change password
✓ Download personal reports
✗ Cannot see other parents' children
✗ Cannot create assessments
✗ Cannot approve enrollments
✗ Cannot manage system settings
✗ Cannot access admin features

Login Route: /login (auto-redirects to dashboard)
Dashboard Features:
- View all enrolled children
- Enrollment status per child
- Quick access to assessments
- Latest report cards
- Pending notifications

================================================================================
DATABASE CONFIGURATION
================================================================================

Database Drivers Supported:
1. SQLite (Default - Local Development)
2. MySQL (Recommended - Production)
3. PostgreSQL (For Large-Scale Apps)
4. SQL Server (Enterprise Environments)

SQLite Configuration (Default):
DB_CONNECTION=sqlite
Database Location: database/database.sqlite
No username/password required
Best for: Local development, testing

MySQL Configuration (Production):
DB_CONNECTION=mysql
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=laravel
DB_USERNAME=root
DB_PASSWORD=(your password)
DB_CHARSET=utf8mb4
DB_COLLATION=utf8mb4_unicode_ci
Strict Mode: Enabled
Foreign Key Constraints: Enabled

PostgreSQL Configuration:
DB_CONNECTION=pgsql
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=5432
DB_DATABASE=laravel
DB_USERNAME=postgres
DB_PASSWORD=(your password)
DB_CHARSET=utf8
Search Path: public

Direct Database Access:

MySQL Connection:
Host: 127.0.0.1 (localhost)
Port: 3306
Username: root
Password: (your MySQL password)
Database: laravel
Charset: utf8mb4

Command Line Access:
mysql -u root -p -h 127.0.0.1
USE laravel;
SHOW TABLES;

SQLite File Access:
Path: /path/to/laravel-project/database/database.sqlite
sqlite3 database/database.sqlite

Database Tables Created:
- users (system user accounts)
- daycares (daycare centers)
- sections (classroom sections)
- students (child enrollment records)
- student_guardians (parent relationships)
- assessments (assessment records)
- assessment_domains (domain definitions)
- eccd_scorings (ECCD assessment scores)
- messages (user messaging)
- sessions (session storage)
- cache (application cache)
- migrations (migration history)

================================================================================
CREATING NEW USER ACCOUNTS
================================================================================

Method 1: Via Admin Dashboard

Create Administrator:
1. Log in as admin
2. Go to Admin > Staff & Users
3. Click "Add New Staff"
4. Select role: Administrator
5. Fill form: Name, Email, Phone
6. Set Status: Active
7. Click "Create User"
8. New admin receives welcome email with temporary password

Create Teacher:
1. Log in as admin
2. Go to Admin > Staff & Users
3. Click "Add New Staff"
4. Select role: Teacher (CDW)
5. Fill form: Name, Email, Phone, Daycare, Section
6. Set Status: Active
7. Click "Create User"
8. Teacher receives welcome email with temporary password

---

Method 2: Parent Self-Registration

1. Navigate to http://localhost:5173/login
2. Click "Don't have an account? Register"
3. Fill registration form:
   - First Name, Middle Name (optional), Last Name
   - Email (must be unique)
   - Phone (format: +63XXXXXXXXXX)
   - Password (8+ chars, uppercase, lowercase, number, special char)
   - Confirm Password
4. Click "Register"
5. Account created immediately
6. Check email for verification link
7. Click verification link to activate
8. Log in to enroll children

---

Method 3: Using Artisan Command Line

Create Admin User:
php artisan tinker
>>> use App\Models\User;
>>> use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Hash;
>>> User::create([
    'email' => 'newadmin@example.com',
    'password' => Hash::make('SecurePassword123!'),
    'role' => 'admin',
    'first_name' => 'John',
    'last_name' => 'Doe',
    'phone' => '+639171234567',
    'status' => 'Active',
    'email_verified_at' => now(),
]);

Create Teacher User:
>>> User::create([
    'email' => 'teacher@example.com',
    'password' => Hash::make('SecurePassword123!'),
    'role' => 'teacher',
    'daycare_id' => 1,
    'first_name' => 'Maria',
    'last_name' => 'Santos',
    'phone' => '+639171234567',
    'status' => 'Active',
    'email_verified_at' => now(),
]);

Create Parent User:
>>> User::create([
    'email' => 'parent@example.com',
    'password' => Hash::make('SecurePassword123!'),
    'role' => 'parent',
    'first_name' => 'Jose',
    'last_name' => 'Garcia',
    'phone' => '+639171234567',
    'status' => 'Active',
    'email_verified_at' => now(),
]);

Password Requirements:
- Minimum 8 characters
- Uppercase letter (A-Z)
- Lowercase letter (a-z)
- Number (0-9)
- Special character (!@#$%^&*)

Email Requirements:
- Valid email format (user@domain.com)
- Must be unique
- Must be verified before full access

